{"type":"message","id":"2be26906","parentId":"149ddd84","timestamp":"2026-03-23T15:44:30.302Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to update the positions. USO was stopped out at 95 (-5% loss), so I need to:\n1. Remove USO from positions (or mark as closed)\n2. Keep A50 with updated price\n3. Update cash (sold USO at 95, got 2850 back)\n4. Add realized P&L from USO loss\n\nLet me calculate:\n- USO: 30 units, bought at 100, sold at 95 = -5% loss = -150 USDT\n- Cash was 4500, now 4500 + 2850 = 7350\n\nWait, let me recalculate properly:\n- Initial capital: 10000\n- Bought USO: 3000 USDT (30 units at 100)\n- Bought A50: 2500 USDT (25 units at 100)\n- Cash: 4500 USDT\n\nUSO stopped out:\n- Sold 30 units at 95 = 2850 USDT\n- Loss: 3000 - 2850 = 150 USDT (-5%)\n- Cash becomes: 4500 + 2850 = 7350 USDT\n\nA50 current:\n- Bought at 100\n- Current price: 96.6 (estimated from 95.16 + 1.5%)\n- Position value: 25 * 96.6 = 2415 USDT\n- Unrealized P&L: 2415 - 2500 = -85 USDT (-3.4%)\n\nTotal equity:\n- Cash: 7350\n- A50 position: 2415\n- Total: 9765 USDT\n\nWait, let me recalculate cash:\nInitial cash after buying: 4500\nSold USO at 95: 30 * 95 = 2850\nCash = 4500 + 2850 = 7350\n\nTotal equity = cash + positions = 7350 + 2415 = 9765 USDT\n\n\nI'll adjust my calculations to match the account details, noting a slight discrepancy in my initial numbers.\n\n- Total equity reveals a complex financial picture with realized and unrealized losses\n- A50 position shows a specific price point and potential strategic positioning\n- Trading parameters indicate a nuanced risk management approach with controlled exposure and leverage","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"019d1b5e3fbc85c130d09ad956efed93","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/workspace/projects/workspace/paper-trading/portfolio.json","newText":"  \"positions\": [\n    {\n      \"symbol\": \"USO\",\n      \"name\": \"United States Oil Fund\",\n      \"si